    <div>
      <p class="book-details">While HIV/AIDS has figured largely in South Africa public discourse over the last ten years, the experiences of people living with HIV remain invisible, and the multiple losses due to AIDS have gone publicly unmourned. This book explores the significance of the disavowal of AIDS-related death, and mourning under apartheid. Stigma and discrimination has minimized spaces for the expression of collective mourning.</p>
